  "scenes": [
    {
      "narration": "Most landlords have a hidden rule that quietly sets the salary you need just to rent. Here it is.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "hook",
          "art": "map",
          "props": [
            "home",
            "coin"
          ],
          "lines": [
            "The salary to",
            "rent here."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The rule is simple. Your annual income must be about forty times the monthly rent to even qualify.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "home",
          "big": "40×",
          "label": "income vs monthly rent",
          "props": [
            "home",
            "lock"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "It's the standard screening rule renters rarely hear about.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-renting",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · renting"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "So a two thousand dollar apartment quietly demands an eighty thousand dollar salary.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "home",
          "big": "$80K",
          "label": "to rent a $2,000 place",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "home"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "In many cities that's roughly double what the median worker earns.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-hai",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · housing affordability"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Which is why, in the biggest cities, rent now demands about twice the median income.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "map",
          "big": "2×",
          "label": "salary needed vs median earned",
          "props": [
            "x",
            "coin"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The median income simply hasn't kept pace with rents.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-medincome",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · median income"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s7"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The same two thousand dollars buys a shared room in one city and a whole house in another.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "Same $2,000, different worlds",
          "props": [
            "home",
            "globe"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s8"
    },
    {
      "narration": "That hidden multiplier prices huge numbers of people out before they even tour a place.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "red",
          "line": "Priced out first",
          "props": [
            "home",
            "x"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s9"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Landlords screen on gross income, before a cent of tax comes out.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-gross",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · gross income"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s10"
    },
    {
      "narration": "So, do you actually earn the salary your city demands?",
      "shots": [
